MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_001: ♪The hunter sends an arrow to pierce the blue sky.\nThe raging beast rises up and lets out a cry!♪
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_002: Ah, so the bewitching voice that drew me here\nwas yours.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_003: Why, hello, Creek. I am honored by your praise.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_004: Those rich, clear tones and enchanting melody are\nthe hallmark of the Blue Rose of Caelus.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_005: But is it the voice of a true prima donna?\nNot quite, I think.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_006: My word, but you are rude. What is this about then?
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_007: There's no need to be upset with me. I have what\nyou need to get the rest of the way there.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_008: YOU have something I need? To improve MY singing\nskills? Please!
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_009: The surest method to improve your singing is to\nembark on a torrid love affair.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_010: And you mean to offer yourself as a suitable partner\nin this endeavor?
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_011: You catch on quickly. One night with me is bound\nto help.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_012: I had heard you were quick to get into romantic\nentanglements. I see now those rumors are true.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_013: That being the case, you must be quite confident in\nyour own singing abilities.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_014: Excuse me?
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_015: If it is true that torrid affairs improve one's singing\nability, then you must be an exquisite vocalist.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_016: That is what you said...is it not?
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_017: Come now, please. Let me hear you sing. I expect\nI shall be mesmerized by the sound of your voice.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_018: Hmm. I wasn't expecting to perform for one so\ntalented today, but I'll do my level best.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_019: Haaah... What did you think?
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_020: That was not at all good. Indeed, it was quite bad.\nDid you really think singing like that could woo me?
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_021: If your many love affairs have created such pitiful\nvocal skills, then clearly you are of no use to me.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_022: Uh... Hehehe. A sharp tongue in a beautiful mouth.
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_023: If you want to win my heart, I suggest you forget the\nsinging lessons and learn instead to be a better man. 
MID_SE_Oly_Hri_C_024: She's tougher than the spoiled rich girl I took her for.\nMore trouble than she's worth, no doubt.